1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,359
A U-100 scale shows one hundred units.

2
00:00:03,359 --> 00:00:04,908
What is a unit, actually?

3
00:00:04,908 --> 00:00:09,622
One unit on a U-100 scale is one hundredth of a milliliter.

4
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:10,403
That's it.

5
00:00:10,403 --> 00:00:13,476
Ten units is zero point one milliliter.

6
00:00:13,476 --> 00:00:17,395
Here's the catch: units measure volume, not peptide.

7
00:00:17,395 --> 00:00:20,403
The amount of peptide depends on the concentration.

8
00:00:20,403 --> 00:00:26,679
At two milligrams per milliliter, zero point one milliliter holds zero point two milligrams.

9
00:00:26,679 --> 00:00:32,473
At five milligrams per milliliter, the same volume holds zero point five milligrams.

10
00:00:32,473 --> 00:00:34,492
Same units, different amount.

11
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:37,591
BuddyPept converts units to milligrams for you.

12
00:00:37,591 --> 00:00:41,341
Free, at Buddy Pept dot com. The math doesn't lie.

13
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:42,578
Follow us for more.

